## Key Model Rules
- **JSONField only** — this is MySQL (Embrella). Never use `ArrayField` (Postgres only).
- `JSONField(default=list)` not `default=[]` — Django evaluates mutable defaults eagerly.
- `deposition_id` and `dataset_id` are nullable until reservation service assigns them. Both have `unique=True`.
- `users.Author` FK is a future dependency — `authors_json` stores only `{author_id, is_primary, is_corresponding, author_list_order}` as raw JSON. No author tables in the depositions app.
- `Deposition` has **no status field** — status is on `Dataset`.
- `DepositionJob` is **OneToOne on Dataset**, not Deposition. Prep and Push run per-dataset.
- All models use `auto_now_add=True` / `auto_now=True` timestamps.
- `submitter_user` uses `SET_NULL` — scientific data must survive user deletion.

---

## Three-Phase Architecture

**Phase 1 — Initialization (SSH)**
- Called from `POST /depositions/v1/sessions/[id]/auto-fill`
- Runs `cryoetportalprep init` via direct SSH (`clusterio.get_cluster_ssh_connection()`)
- Reads MRC headers + AreTomo3 config, returns parsed values to frontend

**Phase 2 — DepositionPrepProcessor (per dataset)**
- Subclasses `BaseProcessor` (same pattern as AreTomo3Processor / DenoisetProcessor)
- One SLURM job: `sync → copick deposit → push --dry-run` (validation only, no upload)
- On success → triggers Phase 3

**Phase 3 — DepositionPushProcessor (per dataset)**
- Subclasses `BaseProcessor`
- Renders its own SLURM script for `aws s3 sync` to `s3://cryoetportal-biohub-hpc-globus/CZII/<dep_id>/<ds_id>/`
- AWS credentials from SSM
- Each dataset goes through its own prep → push, syncing to its own `<dep_id>/<ds_id>/` prefix

Conda env for rendered scripts (via Django setting `DEPOSITION_CONDA_ENV_PATH`):
```
ml load anaconda && conda activate /hpc/projects/group.czii/krios1.processing/software/dataportalenv
```

